From: Caboose <caboose@local>
Subject: [PATCH 66/66] Share device-constant capability answers within an executor session

A GL or Vulkan start asks the same physical-device questions in every process: properties
with their extension chains, queue families and the device's extension list. Each was one round trip to the phone. They now join the
per-session capability cache: each query is wrapped, the original renamed
*_cabooseAsk. A properties chain is kept only when every structure in it is
one the encoder marshals and none holds application pointers; its key is the chain's
shape (each sType and size) and its answer the members after sType and pNext
(caboose-bounded-memory/capability_chains.h). Queue families and extensions are keyed by
the capacity asked for. A process's first properties query is still asked, since it
identifies the device; the tracker's adjustments apply to cached and asked answers alike.
Features and memory properties are not shared: the encoder adjusts them by what the
process has learned about the device (feature emulation, the coherent memory type).
